                                        "entry_id": "1036fb6f-f9f3-3b65-8193-fd621cdf5472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Methyl chloride, a flammable gas once used as a refrigerant, with chemical formula CH₃Cl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36a38445-17de-4425-affd-221a24ff1439",
                                                "sense_id": "b27aa174-2cda-3d30-86ab-03584caebfe9",
                                                "text": "[…] by subjecting that compound to the action of chlorine in sunshine, whereby chloromethane, or methyl chloride, CH₃Cl, is produced, and distilling this chloride with potash."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cd5ff31-2be0-3f30-b706-dcbd7b9ec7b5",
                                        "entry_id": "1036fb6f-f9f3-3b65-8193-fd621cdf5472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the chlorinated derivatives of methane."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af4dc7d3-a8c3-4c5e-9759-27ab6c4b0b9c",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd5ff31-2be0-3f30-b706-dcbd7b9ec7b5",
                                                "text": "Among the halogenated hydrocarbons, chloromethanes (i.e., methyl chloride, CH₃Cl; methylene chloride, CH₂Cl₂; chloroform, CHCl₃; and carbon tetrachloride, CCl₄) play a vital role due to their extensive uses as solvents and chemical intermediates."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
